test: Mia says {r}+{b}+{w}, take em all. nah thats too many. {r} red {b} yellow {w} green balls, eyes closed, least to be sure of {k} same colour
exercise: Since Dad was let go, the power has been cut off, so {a} has to pick socks in the dark. The drawer holds {r} red, {b} blue and {w} white socks. What is the least number {a} must take to be sure of {k} socks of the same colour?
exercise: bloody power's off again cos mum's "between jobs". drawer's got {r} red {b} blue {w} white socks. how many i gotta grab to be sure of {k} the same, it's pitch black
test: The old cat was put to sleep, and its toy box holds {r} red, {b} green and {w} yellow balls. Without looking, how many balls must {a} take out to be certain of {k} of one colour for the new kitten?
exam: A drawer contains {r} red, {b} blue and {w} white socks. Determine the minimum number of socks which must be withdrawn without inspection in order that it be certain that {k} of the socks withdrawn are of the same colour.
exam: It is given that a bag contains {r} red, {b} green and {w} yellow marbles. Ascertain the least number of marbles which {a} must withdraw, without observation, so as to guarantee that no fewer than {k} of them are of one colour.
exam: State the smallest number of pencils which must be taken, without regard to colour, from a box containing {r} black, {b} blue and {w} green pencils, in order to ensure that {k} pencils of an identical colour are obtained.
exam: Whereas a container holds {r} orange, {b} purple and {w} pink balloons, determine the least number of balloons which must be removed blindly in order that the removal of {k} balloons of a single colour be assured.
